AB  - Aircraft maintenance is among the most safety-critical and cost-intensive operation in commercial aviation, where delayed fault detection and fragmented diagnostic workflows can lead to costly Aircraft-On-Ground events and elevated safety risks. In this paper, we review recent advancements across three key AI paradigms: classical machine learning and deep learning (ML/DL), large language models, and multimodal LLMs. These approaches collectively aim to unify visual inspections, high-rate sensor data, and acoustic diagnostics into an integrated decision-support framework. We begin by categorizing over 100 peer-reviewed studies using a generalized taxonomy. We then identify core limitations in existing systems. To address these gaps, we introduce a prototype system that employs Chain-of-Thought prompting with GPT-4o to process synchronized video frames, sensor telemetry, and audio spectrograms, generating per-frame condition labels and maintenance summaries. We evaluate its performance and highlight three key deployment challenges: data fidelity, memory footprint, and modality synchronization. Finally, we outline a roadmap for future research, including the development of standardized multimodal benchmarks, parameter-efficient adaptation techniques, blockchain-based provenance for explainability, and federated inference for privacy-preserving deployment.
